In base \(b\),

\[
17_b = b+7
\]

and

\[
97_b = 9b+7.
\]

We need \(b+7\) to divide \(9b+7\). Rewrite:

\[
9b+7 = 9(b+7)-56.
\]

Thus \(b+7\) must divide \(56\). Since \(b>9\), we have \(b+7>16\). The positive divisors of \(56\) greater than \(16\) are \(28\) and \(56\).

So:

\[
b+7=28 \implies b=21,
\]
\[
b+7=56 \implies b=49.
\]

The sum of all such bases is

\[
21+49=70.
\]

Answer: 70
MODEL_OUTPUT_END

